ed to ___ and start a business."},{"en":"dismiss","id":"WRK-20","kk":"жұмыстан босату","ru":"увольнять","def":"to remove someone from their job","ipa":"dɪsˈmɪs","pos":"v","example":"Staff can be ___ed for stealing."},{"en":"retire","id":"WRK-21","kk":"зейнетке шығу","ru":"выходить на пенсию","def":"to stop working because of age","ipa":"rɪˈtaɪə","pos":"v","example":"Most people ___ at sixty-five."},{"en":"pension","id":"WRK-22","kk":"зейнетақы","ru":"пенсия","def":"money paid to a retired person","ipa":"ˈpenʃn","pos":"n","example":"The state ___ is very low."},{"en":"workforce","id":"WRK-23","kk":"жұмыс күші","ru":"рабочая сила","def":"all the people working in a company or country","ipa":"ˈwɜːkfɔːs","pos":"n","example":"Women make up half the ___."},{"en":"productivity","id":"WRK-24","kk":"өнімділік","ru":"производительность","def":"the amount of work done in a time","ipa":"ˌprɒdʌkˈtɪvəti","pos":"n","example":"Breaks can increase ___."},{"en":"deadline","id":"WRK-25","kk":"соңғы мерзім","ru":"крайний срок","def":"the time by which work must be done","ipa":"ˈdedlaɪn","pos":"n","example":"We missed the ___ by one day."},{"en":"overtime","id":"WRK-26","kk":"үстеме жұмыс","ru":"сверхурочные","def":"work done after normal hours","ipa":"ˈəʊvətaɪm","pos":"n","example":"They are paid extra for ___."},{"en":"commute","id":"WRK-27","kk":"жұмысқа қатынау","ru":"ездить на работу","def":"to travel regularly between home and work","ipa":"kəˈmjuːt","pos":"v","example":"I ___ an hour each way."},{"en":"entrepreneur","id":"WRK-28","kk":"кәсіпкер","ru":"предприниматель","def":"a person who starts a business","ipa":"ˌɒntrəprəˈnɜː","pos":"n","example":"The young ___ opened three cafés."},{"en":"skill","id":"WRK-29","kk":"дағды","ru":"навык","def":"an ability to do something well","ipa":"skɪl","pos":"n","example":"Communication is a key ___."},{"en":"experience","id":"WRK-30","kk":"тәжірибе","ru":"опыт","def":"knowledge gained by doing a job","ipa":"ɪkˈspɪəriəns","pos":"n","example":"T